From b5858c796e90ae419ccd49a6d5c4e82146791a51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:26:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/21] steam-frame client: run the render-pose match off-head
 too (regression probe)

The render-pose match, whose miss rate is the view-shake metric, lives in the
render path, which the runtime skips for an unworn headset: a regression run
with nobody wearing the Frame reported zero misses AND zero hits, a check that
could not fail. In the hidden-session path, peek the newest decoded frame's
PTS (no pixel copy) and match its pose, so the hit/miss counters measure the
pipeline either way. On wake the first rendered frame falls back to the newest
pose once, the same fallback startup uses.

Measured off-head 2026-10-17: 5160 hits, 0 misses over 2.5 min at 25 Mbps
(the hidden loop runs at about 36 Hz, so the probe samples every second frame).

