Subject: [PATCH 05/21] steam-frame client: hand the decoder planes to the GPU,
 convert NV12 in the shader

The client converted every decoded frame NV12 to RGBA on the CPU (sws_scale, SWS_BILINEAR, 2272x1264 at 72 Hz) and then copied the 11.5 MB result twice more on its way to the texture. Now the decoder packs the planes tightly (1.5 bytes/px), the buffers rotate between the two threads instead of being copied, the luma goes up as an R8 image and the chroma as a half-size R8G8 image, and the fragment shader converts with BT.709 limited-range coefficients (what the stream VUI says; swscale default was 601). Measured on the Frame, same build and scene, 25 Mbps: decode call avg 3.5 to 0.6 ms, the convert step 3.1 to 0.5 ms, client process CPU 26 to 10 percent. FRAME_CLIENT_RGBA=1 forces the old path (kept as the fallback for unknown pixel formats). CPU mirror of the shader math and the plane packing are unit-tested (tests/test_yuv.cpp).

