From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:49:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/21] steam-frame client: one GPU submission per frame, no
 CPU wait - two frames in flight

The render thread did three submit-and-wait round trips per frame (upload, eye 0,
eye 1), each queued behind the compositor on the same GPU; worn-session latency
reports showed the eye pass at either about 1 ms or about 10-12 ms, half the samples
each. Now the upload and both eye passes are recorded into one command buffer,
submitted once, and the swapchain images are released without waiting (OpenXR
synchronises Vulkan work on the queue). Two slots with their own staging buffers;
a slot fence is waited only when the slot comes round again. The upload barrier
now orders the overwrite after the previous frame reads (fragment -> transfer).
FRAME_CLIENT_SYNC_GPU=1 keeps a per-frame wait as the fallback. A render thread
line every 300 presented frames breaks the thread time down (memcpy, eyes, fence
wait, xrEndFrame, xrWaitFrame). Verified off-head by readback in both modes (mean
diff 0.4/255); the timing itself needs a wearer.

