+            // Stamp-lead test (2026-10-18, eighth wear): with the stamp honoured, head turns still show the layer one frame
+            // (13.5 ms, r -0.80) behind the overlays. This pulls the stamp BACK along the head's motion by lead_ms, so the
+            // compositor warps the image that much further forward; the lead that zeroes the measured lag is the fixed
+            // offset of the compositor's layer path. Angular velocity is the finite difference of the displayed view pose
+            // (views[0]) over predictedDisplayTime. Positive lead = cures a lag; negative = adds one (the control).
+            // FRAME_CLIENT_STAMP_LEAD_MS sets the start value; /dev/shm/frame-stamp-lead-ms, read once a second, overrides
+            // it live so a wear can try several values without a restart. Each change is logged.
+            {
+                static float leadMs = getenv("FRAME_CLIENT_STAMP_LEAD_MS") ? atof(getenv("FRAME_CLIENT_STAMP_LEAD_MS")) : 0.0f;
+                static float lastLoggedLead = -1e9f;
+                static uint32_t leadPoll = 0;
